%%entity Party help: Root identity for a real-world person or organization; may participate in multiple business roles and has its own lifecycle.
%%field Party.id help: The generated key linking this Party record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Party.party_type help: Whether the identity represents an individual or a legal organization; use the classification consistently when choosing identity evidence.
%%field Party.display_name help: The recognizable name shown when selecting this party for a household, client relationship or nomination.
%%field Party.status enum: PartyStatus
%%field Party.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, deceased, merged. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%% Generator supplies Party.created_at; no custom column is declared.
%% Generator supplies Party.updated_at; no custom column is declared.

%%entity Person help: Individual specialization of Party.
%%field Person.id help: The generated key linking this Person record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Person.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Person.first_name help: The given name on identity evidence; used with the surname to distinguish individual clients.
%%field Person.middle_name help: Additional given names from identity evidence; leave empty where the document contains none.
%%field Person.last_name help: The family name on identity evidence; use the documented spelling when matching client records.
%%field Person.date_of_birth help: The birth date used to distinguish individuals and assess age-dependent planning horizons.
%%field Person.gender help: The party's supplied demographic description; do not infer it from the name.
%%field Person.marital_status help: The individual's supplied family circumstances: single, married, partnered, separated, divorced or widowed; not_disclosed retains the choice not to provide this demographic information.
%%field Person.nationality help: The citizenship recorded in identity evidence; distinguish it from tax residence and postal country.
%%field Person.occupation help: The individual's current work or profession, used when discussing income stability and financial circumstances.

%%entity Organization help: Legal-entity specialization of Party, including companies, trusts, partnerships, HUFs and institutions.
%%field Organization.id help: The generated key linking this Organization record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Organization.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Organization.legal_name help: The registered name on legal and tax evidence rather than an informal trading abbreviation.
%%field Organization.organization_type help: The legal form, such as company, trust or partnership, used to identify the relevant ownership and evidence requirements.
%%field Organization.registration_number help: The registration reference issued to the organization or regulated provider; retain the issuing authority's spelling.
%%field Organization.tax_identifier help: The legal party's taxpayer reference used when matching tax declarations and account documentation.

%%entity Household help: Primary consolidated wealth context for related parties and clients.
%%field Household.id help: The generated key linking this Household record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Household.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Household.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field Household.primary_advisor_id help: The lead adviser accountable for this household relationship, distinct from relationship-management support.
%%field Household.relationship_manager_reference help: The adviser coordinating ongoing household service and follow-up, separate from the lead adviser, recorded as the adviser's employee number. A reference rather than a link: the lead adviser is the household's one linked adviser, and this second role is not enforced against the advisor table.
%%field Household.risk_profile_id help: The approved risk context used when assessing this household or portfolio; retain the applicable version for later review.
%%field Household.annual_income help: The household's annual income in its planning currency; keep the period and gross or net basis consistent across reviews.
%%field Household.net_worth help: Household assets less liabilities in the planning currency at the reviewed valuation date.
%% Generator supplies Household.created_at; no custom column is declared.

%%entity HouseholdMember help: Time-bounded association of a Party with a Household.
%%field HouseholdMember.id help: The generated key linking this HouseholdMember record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field HouseholdMember.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field HouseholdMember.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field HouseholdMember.relationship_type help: How the related parties are connected, distinguishing family membership from beneficiary or ownership relationships.
%%field HouseholdMember.ownership_percentage help: The share attributable to this member, expressed on a 0 to 100 scale; this is ownership rather than the member's allocation target.
%%field HouseholdMember.is_primary help: Selects the preferred membership, address or account within its owner; review other primary selections before enabling it.
%%field HouseholdMember.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field HouseholdMember.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.

%%entity Client help: Onboarded advisory or distribution relationship for a Party within a Household.
%%field Client.id help: The generated key linking this Client record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Client.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Client.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field Client.client_number help: The stable business reference for this client relationship, used when matching service requests and external records.
%%field Client.client_type help: The client relationship's legal or commercial classification used when choosing onboarding and service requirements.
%%field Client.status enum: ClientStatus
%%field Client.status help: Allowed values are prospect, onboarding, pending_kyc, active, suspended, inactive, closed. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field Client.onboarding_date help: The day the client relationship was established, rather than the date the prospect first contacted the adviser.
%%field Client.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field Client.service_model help: The agreed advisory or distribution service arrangement that determines the work the client expects.
%%field Client.fee_model help: The agreed basis for charging this client; distinguish advisory charges from product commissions.

%%entity Address help: A postal location used for client correspondence and identity evidence. Keep registered and correspondence locations separate so changing delivery details does not overwrite KYC evidence.
%%field Address.id help: The generated key linking this Address record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Address.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Address.address_type help: The purpose of this location, such as registered residence or correspondence, so mailing changes do not overwrite legal evidence.
%%field Address.line1 help: Street and building details needed for delivery and identification matching.
%%field Address.city help: The municipality used for postal delivery and location matching, separate from the wider region.
%%field Address.region help: The geographical state or province of the postal address; this is free text rather than a record lifecycle.
%%field Address.postal_code help: The postal sorting reference for the address, retained as text to preserve leading zeroes.
%%field Address.country help: The country relevant to this address or declaration; distinguish physical location from citizenship.
%%field Address.is_primary help: Selects the preferred membership, address or account within its owner; review other primary selections before enabling it.

%%entity ContactPoint help: A way to reach a party, such as email or telephone. Verification records whether the contact has been confirmed; the primary flag selects the preferred channel.
%%field ContactPoint.id help: The generated key linking this ContactPoint record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ContactPoint.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field ContactPoint.contact_type help: The communication channel, such as telephone or email, that determines how the stored value is used.
%%field ContactPoint.value help: The supplied evidence or assumption content; interpret it together with its classification and unit rather than as an unqualified number.
%%field ContactPoint.is_primary help: Selects the preferred membership, address or account within its owner; review other primary selections before enabling it.
%%field ContactPoint.verified help: Indicates that the supplied contact channel has been confirmed; false includes channels still awaiting confirmation.

%%entity Nominee help: A beneficiary designated by a client, with an effective period and a share of the nominated entitlement. It records a nomination rather than a transfer of present ownership.
%%field Nominee.id help: The generated key linking this Nominee record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Nominee.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field Nominee.nominee_party_id help: The legal identity designated as beneficiary, rather than the client making the nomination.
%%field Nominee.relationship_type help: How the related parties are connected, distinguishing family membership from beneficiary or ownership relationships.
%%field Nominee.allocation_percentage help: The nominated beneficiary's share on a 0 to 100 scale; review the total across nominees before accepting the designation.
%%field Nominee.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field Nominee.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.

%%entity PowerOfAttorney help: Authority granted by one party to another to act within a stated scope and effective period. The scope must be checked before accepting instructions on the grantor's behalf.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.id help: The generated key linking this PowerOfAttorney record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.grantor_party_id help: The party granting authority, whose instructions may be given only within the recorded scope.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.attorney_party_reference help: The party authorised to act for the grantor, recorded as that party's display name or client number. A reference rather than a link: the grantor is the one linked party, and this is not ownership of the grantor's assets.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.effective_date help: The first day the authority, plan or risk context may be relied upon; keep earlier decisions tied to the version then in force.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.status help: Allowed values are draft, active, expired, revoked. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field PowerOfAttorney.scope help: The instructions the attorney may give on the grantor's behalf; do not treat this authority as unrestricted.

%%entity OrganizationUnit help: A branch or department within the advisory organization. Its parent link permits a hierarchy used to assign advisers and teams.
%%field OrganizationUnit.id help: The generated key linking this OrganizationUnit record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field OrganizationUnit.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field OrganizationUnit.unit_type help: The organizational level, such as branch or department, used when placing advisers in the hierarchy.
%%field OrganizationUnit.organization_unit_id help: The organizational unit immediately above this one; leave empty at the root of the hierarchy.
%%field OrganizationUnit.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity Advisor help: An adviser associated with a party and organizational unit, carrying employment and licence references used when assigning client responsibility.
%%field Advisor.id help: The generated key linking this Advisor record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Advisor.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Advisor.organization_unit_id help: The branch or department responsible for the adviser or team, used to organize service responsibilities.
%%field Advisor.employee_number help: The adviser reference assigned by the employer, used to reconcile assignments without relying on a person's name.
%%field Advisor.advisor_type help: The adviser's service capacity, used when assigning responsibilities and reviewing licence coverage.
%%field Advisor.license_number help: The professional authorization reference used to verify that the adviser may provide the relevant service.
%%field Advisor.license_expiry help: The date the recorded professional authorization must be renewed; it is independent of employment status.
%%field Advisor.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, suspended. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity AdvisorAssignment parent: Advisor
%%entity AdvisorAssignment help: A dated allocation of an adviser to a household. Retaining ended assignments shows who was responsible when advice was issued.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.id help: The generated key linking this AdvisorAssignment record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.assignment_type help: The capacity in which the adviser serves this household, such as lead adviser or relationship support.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field AdvisorAssignment.is_primary help: Selects the preferred membership, address or account within its owner; review other primary selections before enabling it.

%%entity Team help: A named working group within an organizational unit. Membership is maintained separately so staffing changes do not erase historical assignments.
%%field Team.id help: The generated key linking this Team record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Team.organization_unit_id help: The branch or department responsible for the adviser or team, used to organize service responsibilities.
%%field Team.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Team.team_type help: The working group's service function, used to distinguish client coverage from specialist review.
%%field Team.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity TeamMember help: A dated association of an adviser with a working group, including the capacity in which the adviser participates.
%%field TeamMember.id help: The generated key linking this TeamMember record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field TeamMember.team_id help: The working group within which the adviser holds this dated membership.
%%field TeamMember.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field TeamMember.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field TeamMember.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field TeamMember.role help: The capacity in which the adviser participates in this team; this is a membership description rather than a system permission grant.

%%entity Prospect help: A potential client being qualified by an assigned adviser. Source, estimated assets and the next contact date support follow-up before onboarding.
%%field Prospect.id help: The generated key linking this Prospect record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Prospect.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Prospect.source help: Where the prospect, evidence or observation originated; retain enough detail to trace the business basis of the record.
%%field Prospect.status enum: ProspectStatus
%%field Prospect.status help: Allowed values are new, contacted, qualified, meeting, proposal, converted, lost. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field Prospect.lead_score help: The qualification score supplied for the prospect; interpret it using the organization's scoring scale rather than as invested assets.
%%field Prospect.assigned_advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for qualifying this prospect or completing this onboarding case.
%%field Prospect.estimated_aum help: The prospect's estimated assets available for management in the relevant currency; this is an estimate rather than a reconciled portfolio value.
%%field Prospect.next_action_date help: The next planned follow-up with the prospect, used to identify opportunities that have stalled.

%%entity Interaction help: A dated conversation or contact with a party. Subject and notes retain the context of advice and client instructions rather than merely recording that contact occurred.
%%field Interaction.id help: The generated key linking this Interaction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Interaction.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Interaction.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field Interaction.interaction_type help: The communication or meeting channel used for this contact, distinguishing advice discussions from routine correspondence.
%%field Interaction.interaction_at help: When the conversation or contact took place, rather than when its notes were entered.
%%field Interaction.subject help: A concise description that lets the adviser distinguish this interaction, task or request in a work list.
%%field Interaction.notes help: The substance of the discussion or follow-up, including relevant instructions and unresolved questions.

%%entity Activity help: A work item assigned to an adviser for a client. Due date, priority and completion timestamp distinguish planned follow-up from work actually completed.
%%field Activity.id help: The generated key linking this Activity record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Activity.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field Activity.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field Activity.activity_type help: The kind of adviser work required, used to distinguish meetings, document collection and other follow-up.
%%field Activity.subject help: A concise description that lets the adviser distinguish this interaction, task or request in a work list.
%%field Activity.due_date help: The deadline for the assigned work; passing it does not itself record completion.
%%field Activity.priority help: The business urgency used to order follow-up; apply the same priority scale across client work.
%%field Activity.status help: Allowed values are planned, in_progress, completed, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field Activity.completed_at help: When the requested work was actually finished; leave empty while it remains open.

%%entity ServiceRequest help: A client request tracked from submission through assignment, processing and resolution. Completion records when the service was delivered, not when the request was received.
%%field ServiceRequest.id help: The generated key linking this ServiceRequest record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ServiceRequest.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field ServiceRequest.request_type help: The service the client is asking for, used to route the request to the responsible business role.
%%field ServiceRequest.subject help: A concise description that lets the adviser distinguish this interaction, task or request in a work list.
%%field ServiceRequest.status enum: ServiceRequestStatus
%%field ServiceRequest.status help: Allowed values are submitted, assigned, processing, awaiting_client, completed, rejected. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field ServiceRequest.priority help: The business urgency used to order follow-up; apply the same priority scale across client work.
%%field ServiceRequest.submitted_at help: When the client request was received, used to measure elapsed service time.
%%field ServiceRequest.completed_at help: When the requested work was actually finished; leave empty while it remains open.

%%entity OnboardingCase help: The work required to establish a client relationship from a prospect. KYC, suitability and approval are stages of this case, and cancellation retains the unsuccessful attempt.
%%field OnboardingCase.id help: The generated key linking this OnboardingCase record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field OnboardingCase.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field OnboardingCase.prospect_id help: The qualified opportunity from which this onboarding case originated.
%%field OnboardingCase.status enum: OnboardingStatus
%%field OnboardingCase.status help: Allowed values are started, kyc, suitability, approval, active, rejected, cancelled. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field OnboardingCase.started_date help: When the onboarding case began; this is separate from activation of the client relationship.
%%field OnboardingCase.completed_date help: When onboarding work was completed; keep empty for an unfinished or abandoned case.
%%field OnboardingCase.assigned_advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for qualifying this prospect or completing this onboarding case.

%%entity KYCRecord help: The client identification and verification record, including evidence references and an expiry date. Expiry requires renewed verification rather than deleting earlier evidence.
%%field KYCRecord.id help: The generated key linking this KYCRecord record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field KYCRecord.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field KYCRecord.kyc_status help: Allowed values are pending, in_review, verified, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field KYCRecord.kyc_type help: The identification procedure or evidence set applied to this client, used when reviewing verification coverage.
%%field KYCRecord.verification_date help: The day the identification evidence was accepted, providing the starting point for later renewal review.
%%field KYCRecord.verification_source help: The officer, provider or evidence source supporting the verification result; retain a traceable reference.
%%field KYCRecord.kyc_identifier help: The external identification reference used to match this client to the verification evidence.
%%field KYCRecord.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.

%%entity KYCVerification help: One verification performed against a client identification record. Keep its source and reference so an officer can trace the evidence supporting a verified outcome.
%%field KYCVerification.id help: The generated key linking this KYCVerification record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field KYCVerification.kyc_record_id help: The identification evidence record this individual verification supports.
%%field KYCVerification.verification_type help: The check performed against the supplied evidence, such as identity or bank-account confirmation.
%%field KYCVerification.status help: Allowed values are pending, in_review, verified, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field KYCVerification.verified_at help: When this verification outcome was recorded; empty means no completed check has been evidenced.
%%field KYCVerification.verification_source help: The officer, provider or evidence source supporting the verification result; retain a traceable reference.
%%field KYCVerification.reference_number help: The evidence provider's business reference used to trace this check rather than an internal database key.

%%entity FATCADeclaration help: A client declaration of tax residency and US-person status retained as identification evidence for the relevant reporting assessment.
%%field FATCADeclaration.id help: The generated key linking this FATCADeclaration record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field FATCADeclaration.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field FATCADeclaration.tax_residency help: The client's declared tax residence for the reporting assessment; it may differ from citizenship and mailing address.
%%field FATCADeclaration.country help: The country relevant to this address or declaration; distinguish physical location from citizenship.
%%field FATCADeclaration.tin help: The taxpayer number declared for the stated country; preserve formatting needed to match the declaration evidence.
%%field FATCADeclaration.us_person help: The client's declared US-person indicator used in the tax-reporting assessment; do not infer it from postal address alone.
%%field FATCADeclaration.declaration_date help: When the client made this declaration; retain the date associated with the supplied evidence.

%%entity CRSDeclaration help: A dated client statement of tax residency and taxpayer reference for common reporting assessment. Retain its country and declaration status together.
%%field CRSDeclaration.id help: The generated key linking this CRSDeclaration record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field CRSDeclaration.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field CRSDeclaration.tax_residency help: The client's declared tax residence for the reporting assessment; it may differ from citizenship and mailing address.
%%field CRSDeclaration.country help: The country relevant to this address or declaration; distinguish physical location from citizenship.
%%field CRSDeclaration.tin help: The taxpayer number declared for the stated country; preserve formatting needed to match the declaration evidence.
%%field CRSDeclaration.declaration_date help: When the client made this declaration; retain the date associated with the supplied evidence.
%%field CRSDeclaration.status help: Allowed values are draft, submitted, verified, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity SuitabilityAssessment help: An assessment of whether the proposed service or investment fits the client's circumstances. The assessor and dated outcome provide the evidence behind the suitability decision.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.id help: The generated key linking this SuitabilityAssessment record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.assessment_type help: The kind of risk or suitability evaluation performed, used to distinguish the purpose of the recorded result.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.assessment_date help: The date the client's circumstances were evaluated; later advice should consider whether they have changed.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.status help: Allowed values are draft, in_review, completed, expired. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.result help: The recorded outcome of this assessment or projection, supported by the referenced evidence and explanation.
%%field SuitabilityAssessment.assessor_id help: The adviser or authorized reviewer who performed the suitability evaluation; preserve the identity behind the decision.

%%entity IdentityDocument help: Identity evidence supplied by a party, with issue and expiry dates and a verification outcome. An expired document remains part of the evidence history.
%%field IdentityDocument.id help: The generated key linking this IdentityDocument record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field IdentityDocument.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field IdentityDocument.document_type help: The evidence classification, such as identity or authorization, used when checking whether the required document was supplied.
%%field IdentityDocument.document_number help: The reference printed on the supplied identity evidence; retain it separately from the file's internal key.
%%field IdentityDocument.issue_date help: When the issuing authority created the evidence, not when it was uploaded to this system.
%%field IdentityDocument.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.
%%field IdentityDocument.verification_status help: Allowed values are pending, in_review, verified, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity ESignatureRequest help: A request for a client to sign a stored document. Provider reference links the request to signing evidence, while signed_at is empty until a signature is received.
%%field ESignatureRequest.id help: The generated key linking this ESignatureRequest record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ESignatureRequest.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field ESignatureRequest.document_id help: The stored document the client is being asked to sign; retain the exact issued revision.
%%field ESignatureRequest.status help: Allowed values are requested, sent, signed, declined, expired, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field ESignatureRequest.requested_at help: When the client was asked to sign, used to distinguish a pending request from received evidence.
%%field ESignatureRequest.signed_at help: When a completed signature was evidenced; leave empty until the signing provider confirms it.
%%field ESignatureRequest.provider_reference help: The signing service's reference used to retrieve or reconcile signature evidence.

%%entity BankAccount help: A client bank account used when validating funding or payout details. Verification status distinguishes supplied account information from a confirmed settlement destination.
%%field BankAccount.id help: The generated key linking this BankAccount record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field BankAccount.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field BankAccount.bank_name help: The institution holding the client's account, as supplied on bank evidence.
%%field BankAccount.account_number help: The institution's account reference, stored as text to retain leading zeroes and provider formatting.
%%field BankAccount.account_type help: The provider's account classification, used to distinguish settlement and investment account purposes.
%%field BankAccount.ifsc help: The Indian branch routing code supplied for settlement; retain the code from bank evidence.
%%field BankAccount.branch help: The bank branch identified on the account documentation, used when matching settlement details.
%%field BankAccount.is_primary help: Selects the preferred membership, address or account within its owner; review other primary selections before enabling it.
%%field BankAccount.verification_status help: Allowed values are pending, in_review, verified, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity Document help: A stored item of party evidence or correspondence, identified by its filename, classification and retrievable location. Its upload timestamp records receipt of evidence.
%%field Document.id help: The generated key linking this Document record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Document.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field Document.document_type help: What kind of evidence this is — passport, national_id, proof_of_address, tax_return, bank_statement, kyc_form, signed_agreement or other. The review queue and the KYC checks key on it, so choose the narrowest class that is true.
%%field Document.file_name help: The original evidence filename shown to a reviewer; a filename alone does not establish that evidence is verified.
%%field Document.document_url help: The retrievable location of the stored evidence; access must follow the document's business permissions.
%%field Document.status help: Allowed values are received, in_review, verified, rejected, archived. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field Document.uploaded_at help: When evidence was received into the document register, distinct from its issue or signature date.

%%entity AuditEvent help: Append-only business audit event capturing who, what, when and before/after values.
%%field AuditEvent.id help: The generated key linking this AuditEvent record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AuditEvent.timestamp help: When the audited business operation occurred; use the event time rather than a later export time.
%%field AuditEvent.user_reference help: Who performed the audited operation, as the platform identifies its users. A reference rather than a link: the sign-in directory is not part of this model, and an audit entry has to outlive the account it names.
%%field AuditEvent.action help: The operation recorded by the audit event, such as creation, correction or status change.
%%field AuditEvent.entity_type help: The business record classification affected by this event, used with entity_reference to identify the subject.
%%field AuditEvent.entity_reference help: The affected record's key interpreted together with entity_type; it is polymorphic text rather than a foreign key to one table.
%%field AuditEvent.before_value help: The retained value before the audited change; empty may represent a new record with no previous value.
%%field AuditEvent.after_value help: The retained value after the audited change, used with before_value to understand what was altered.
%%field AuditEvent.source help: Where the prospect, evidence or observation originated; retain enough detail to trace the business basis of the record.
%%field AuditEvent.ip_address help: The network address associated with the operation, retained as context rather than as proof of a person's identity.
%%field AuditEvent.correlation_reference help: The shared request or process reference linking related audit events; it is not a business-table foreign key.

%%entity FinancialPlan help: Versioned household financial plan describing objectives, assumptions, scenarios and funding requirements.
%%field FinancialPlan.id help: The generated key linking this FinancialPlan record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field FinancialPlan.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field FinancialPlan.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field FinancialPlan.plan_number help: The business reference used to distinguish this household plan from other planning engagements.
%%field FinancialPlan.plan_version help: The revision of the household planning assumptions, used to keep earlier advice traceable after a new plan is approved.
%%field FinancialPlan.status enum: PlanStatus
%%field FinancialPlan.status help: Allowed values are draft, analysis, proposed, approved, active, superseded, archived. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field FinancialPlan.effective_date help: The first day the authority, plan or risk context may be relied upon; keep earlier decisions tied to the version then in force.
%%field FinancialPlan.review_date help: The planned or actual review date, interpreted in the context of this plan or client-review record.
%%field FinancialPlan.base_currency help: The currency in which this plan or portfolio combines monetary values; convert foreign-currency amounts before aggregation.

%%entity FinancialPlanAssumption help: One assumption underlying a financial plan, retained with its value, unit and source so projections can be reviewed and reproduced.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.id help: The generated key linking this FinancialPlanAssumption record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.assumption_type help: The planning variable being assumed, such as growth, inflation or a recurring commitment; interpret the stored value with its unit.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.value help: The supplied evidence or assumption content; interpret it together with its classification and unit rather than as an unqualified number.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.unit help: The measurement basis for the assumption, such as annual percent or monthly currency amount.
%%field FinancialPlanAssumption.source help: Where the prospect, evidence or observation originated; retain enough detail to trace the business basis of the record.

%%entity IncomeSource help: A dated stream of household income used in a plan. Amount and frequency must be considered together when calculating available savings.
%%field IncomeSource.id help: The generated key linking this IncomeSource record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field IncomeSource.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field IncomeSource.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field IncomeSource.income_type help: The source of household receipts, distinguishing salary, business income and investment income in the plan.
%%field IncomeSource.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field IncomeSource.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field IncomeSource.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field IncomeSource.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field IncomeSource.inflation_linked help: Indicates that projected amounts follow the plan's inflation assumption rather than remaining fixed over time.

%%entity Expense help: A planned outflow with a recurrence and effective period. Inflation linkage distinguishes expenses that rise with an assumed cost index from fixed commitments.
%%field Expense.id help: The generated key linking this Expense record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Expense.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field Expense.expense_type help: The household spending classification used to separate recurring living costs from other planned outflows.
%%field Expense.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field Expense.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field Expense.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field Expense.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field Expense.inflation_linked help: Indicates that projected amounts follow the plan's inflation assumption rather than remaining fixed over time.

%%entity Liability help: A debt included in the household plan, carrying outstanding principal, borrowing cost and repayment timing. It reduces the wealth available to fund goals.
%%field Liability.id help: The generated key linking this Liability record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Liability.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field Liability.liability_type help: The borrowing category used when reviewing debt costs, repayment obligations and the effect on net wealth.
%%field Liability.outstanding_amount help: The remaining debt principal in the plan's currency at the review date, excluding amounts already repaid.
%%field Liability.interest_rate help: The borrowing rate expressed as annual percent unless the debt contract states another basis; record that basis consistently.
%%field Liability.maturity_date help: The contractual date principal falls due or the debt instrument matures; it is not a forecast sale date.
%%field Liability.monthly_payment help: The contractual monthly repayment in the liability's currency, used in household cash-flow projections.
%%field Liability.status help: Allowed values are active, settled, defaulted, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity CashFlow help: A dated inflow or outflow used in planning calculations. Category and recurrence explain which budget assumption produced the projected amount.
%%field CashFlow.id help: The generated key linking this CashFlow record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field CashFlow.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field CashFlow.cashflow_type help: Whether this planning item is an inflow or outflow and its financial purpose, used when constructing the projected cash balance.
%%field CashFlow.category help: The financial grouping used for this assumption, product or cash flow; apply the same grouping when comparing periods.
%%field CashFlow.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field CashFlow.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field CashFlow.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field CashFlow.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field CashFlow.inflation_linked help: Indicates that projected amounts follow the plan's inflation assumption rather than remaining fixed over time.

%%entity Goal help: Financial objective tracked through planning, funding and achievement.
%%field Goal.id help: The generated key linking this Goal record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Goal.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field Goal.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field Goal.goal_type help: The purpose of the household objective, such as education, retirement or a planned purchase, used when reviewing funding priorities.
%%field Goal.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Goal.target_amount help: The required goal value in the plan's currency at the target date; distinguish future-cost assumptions from today's quoted cost.
%%field Goal.target_date help: When the household expects to need the goal funding, which determines the investment horizon.
%%field Goal.priority help: The business urgency used to order follow-up; apply the same priority scale across client work.
%%field Goal.status enum: GoalStatus
%%field Goal.status help: Allowed values are identified, planned, funded, achieved, cancelled. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field Goal.funded_percentage help: The proportion of the required goal value currently covered, expressed on a 0 to 100 scale.

%%entity GoalFunding help: An allocation of an investment, portfolio or cash flow toward a goal. It records earmarking and does not itself move money or execute a trade.
%%field GoalFunding.id help: The generated key linking this GoalFunding record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field GoalFunding.goal_id help: The household objective whose funding or projection this row explains.
%%field GoalFunding.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field GoalFunding.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field GoalFunding.cashflow_id help: The planned receipt or payment earmarked toward this goal; the intended target is CashFlow.
%%field GoalFunding.allocated_amount help: The amount earmarked toward this goal in the plan's currency; earmarking does not itself settle a transaction.

%%entity GoalProjection help: A forecast for a goal under a selected scenario. Projected value and shortfall show how the funding assumptions compare with the required target.
%%field GoalProjection.id help: The generated key linking this GoalProjection record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field GoalProjection.goal_id help: The household objective whose funding or projection this row explains.
%%field GoalProjection.scenario_id help: The alternative planning assumptions used for this forecast rather than the baseline plan.
%%field GoalProjection.projection_date help: The forecast date against which the goal outcome was calculated; compare forecasts made with the same planning assumptions.
%%field GoalProjection.projected_value help: The expected value available for the goal in the plan's currency under this scenario.
%%field GoalProjection.shortfall help: The amount by which projected funding falls below the goal requirement in the same currency; distinguish it from the entire target.
%%field GoalProjection.result help: The recorded outcome of this assessment or projection, supported by the referenced evidence and explanation.

%%entity Scenario help: An alternative set of assumptions for a financial plan. Comparing scenarios makes the sensitivity of goal funding visible without replacing the approved plan.
%%field Scenario.id help: The generated key linking this Scenario record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Scenario.financial_plan_id help: The household plan whose assumptions or commitments this record contributes to; do not combine rows from different plan revisions.
%%field Scenario.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Scenario.scenario_type help: The interpretation of the alternate assumptions, such as baseline or stress case, used when comparing forecasts.
%%field Scenario.status help: Allowed values are draft, active, superseded, archived. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field Scenario.description help: The business explanation of this scenario or allocation model, including which assumptions distinguish it from alternatives.

%%entity ScenarioAssumption help: An override used only by its scenario. Value and unit explain how that forecast differs from the plan's baseline assumptions.
%%field ScenarioAssumption.id help: The generated key linking this ScenarioAssumption record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ScenarioAssumption.scenario_id help: The alternative planning assumptions used for this forecast rather than the baseline plan.
%%field ScenarioAssumption.assumption_type help: The planning variable being assumed, such as growth, inflation or a recurring commitment; interpret the stored value with its unit.
%%field ScenarioAssumption.value help: The supplied evidence or assumption content; interpret it together with its classification and unit rather than as an unqualified number.
%%field ScenarioAssumption.unit help: The measurement basis for the assumption, such as annual percent or monthly currency amount.

%%entity RiskAssessment help: A dated evaluation of a client or household's capacity and willingness to take investment risk. Its result is evidence used to prepare a risk profile.
%%field RiskAssessment.id help: The generated key linking this RiskAssessment record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RiskAssessment.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field RiskAssessment.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field RiskAssessment.assessment_date help: The date the client's circumstances were evaluated; later advice should consider whether they have changed.
%%field RiskAssessment.assessment_type help: The kind of risk or suitability evaluation performed, used to distinguish the purpose of the recorded result.
%%field RiskAssessment.status help: draft is not yet evaluated; assessed records an evaluation; approved authorizes its use as risk evidence; expired and superseded retain assessments that should no longer guide new advice.
%%field RiskAssessment.result help: The recorded outcome of this assessment or projection, supported by the referenced evidence and explanation.

%%entity RiskProfile help: Approved risk context used when evaluating recommendations; historical versions are retained.
%%field RiskProfile.id help: The generated key linking this RiskProfile record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RiskProfile.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field RiskProfile.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field RiskProfile.risk_score help: The assessment score used to derive the risk classification; retain the assessment's scale and effective date.
%%field RiskProfile.risk_category enum: RiskCategory
%%field RiskProfile.risk_category help: Allowed values are conservative, moderately_conservative, moderate, moderately_aggressive, aggressive. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field RiskProfile.effective_date help: The first day the authority, plan or risk context may be relied upon; keep earlier decisions tied to the version then in force.
%%field RiskProfile.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.
%%field RiskProfile.assessment_id help: The retained assessment evidence supporting this risk or suitability result; this reference needs an unambiguous model relationship.
%%field RiskProfile.status enum: RiskStatus
%%field RiskProfile.status help: Allowed values are draft, assessed, approved, expired, superseded. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity RiskProfileHistory help: A retained version of a risk profile and its effective period. The reason explains why advice should use a newer profile instead of the previous one.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.id help: The generated key linking this RiskProfileHistory record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.risk_profile_id help: The approved risk context used when assessing this household or portfolio; retain the applicable version for later review.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.risk_score help: The assessment score used to derive the risk classification; retain the assessment's scale and effective date.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.risk_category enum: RiskCategory
%%field RiskProfileHistory.risk_category help: Allowed values are conservative, moderately_conservative, moderate, moderately_aggressive, aggressive. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.effective_date help: The first day the authority, plan or risk context may be relied upon; keep earlier decisions tied to the version then in force.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.
%%field RiskProfileHistory.reason help: The explanation for this allocation, assessment change or exception; retain enough context for an adviser to review the decision later.

%%entity Security help: An investable instrument identified by name, symbol and optional ISIN. Currency and classification are needed before comparing prices or combining holdings.
%%field Security.id help: The generated key linking this Security record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Security.security_type_id help: The instrument classification that determines how this security is valued and reviewed.
%%field Security.symbol help: The market or provider shorthand used to locate the investment instrument; distinguish it from a global identifier.
%%field Security.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Security.isin help: The instrument's international identification reference used to match holdings and product records.
%%field Security.currency help: The instrument's quoted or settlement currency; it may differ from the portfolio's reporting currency.
%%field Security.status help: Allowed values are active, suspended, matured, delisted. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity SecurityType help: A classification of investable instruments, used to distinguish products with different valuation, execution or suitability characteristics.
%%field SecurityType.id help: The generated key linking this SecurityType record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SecurityType.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field SecurityType.category help: The financial grouping used for this assumption, product or cash flow; apply the same grouping when comparing periods.
%%field SecurityType.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity MutualFundScheme help: A specific fund scheme, plan and option managed by an AMC. Scheme code and ISIN distinguish products whose names may otherwise appear similar.
%%field MutualFundScheme.id help: The generated key linking this MutualFundScheme record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field MutualFundScheme.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field MutualFundScheme.amc_id help: The asset management company responsible for the scheme and its product documentation.
%%field MutualFundScheme.scheme_code help: The fund provider's stable scheme reference, used to match prices and transactions without relying on a similar product name.
%%field MutualFundScheme.isin help: The instrument's international identification reference used to match holdings and product records.
%%field MutualFundScheme.scheme_name help: The provider's marketed scheme name; plan and option must also be checked before identifying the investable product.
%%field MutualFundScheme.category help: The financial grouping used for this assumption, product or cash flow; apply the same grouping when comparing periods.
%%field MutualFundScheme.plan_type help: The fund distribution or pricing plan selected for this scheme; different plans can have different charges.
%%field MutualFundScheme.option_type help: The fund's income or accumulation option, used to distinguish products sharing the same underlying scheme.
%%field MutualFundScheme.benchmark help: The comparison series selected for this fund; retain the provider's reference when assessing relative returns.
%%field MutualFundScheme.risk_level help: The product's disclosed risk classification, used alongside the client's own risk capacity during suitability review.

%%entity AMC help: The asset management company responsible for fund schemes. Registration reference supports verification of the legal manager behind the product.
%%field AMC.id help: The generated key linking this AMC record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AMC.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field AMC.registration_number help: The registration reference issued to the organization or regulated provider; retain the issuing authority's spelling.
%%field AMC.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity ProductPrice help: An observed price for a security on a stated date. Price type and source distinguish an official valuation from another market observation.
%%field ProductPrice.id help: The generated key linking this ProductPrice record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ProductPrice.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field ProductPrice.price_date help: The date the observation applies to; do not value a portfolio using an undated or mismatched price.
%%field ProductPrice.price help: The amount per instrument unit in its quote currency at the observation or transaction date.
%%field ProductPrice.price_type help: The basis of the observation, such as closing quote or net asset value, needed when comparing sources.
%%field ProductPrice.source help: Where the prospect, evidence or observation originated; retain enough detail to trace the business basis of the record.

%%entity AssetClass help: A grouping used to set allocation targets and compare exposure. A parent classification permits a broad class to contain narrower investment groups.
%%field AssetClass.id help: The generated key linking this AssetClass record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AssetClass.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field AssetClass.asset_class_id help: The broader investment classification containing this class; leave empty for a top-level class.
%%field AssetClass.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity InvestmentAccount help: A client account held with an investment institution. Ownership and opening details determine which holdings may be consolidated into a portfolio.
%%field InvestmentAccount.id help: The generated key linking this InvestmentAccount record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field InvestmentAccount.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field InvestmentAccount.institution_id help: The provider holding the investment account; the uploaded model does not declare an Institution master.
%%field InvestmentAccount.account_number help: The institution's account reference, stored as text to retain leading zeroes and provider formatting.
%%field InvestmentAccount.account_type help: The provider's account classification, used to distinguish settlement and investment account purposes.
%%field InvestmentAccount.ownership_type help: The account's legal holding arrangement, such as sole or joint, used when consolidating client wealth.
%%field InvestmentAccount.opened_date help: When the provider account began, not when its record was first imported into the portfolio.
%%field InvestmentAccount.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, suspended, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity Folio help: A mutual fund investor reference associated with an investment account and scheme. Use the provider's folio number when reconciling fund records.
%%field Folio.id help: The generated key linking this Folio record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Folio.investment_account_id help: The provider account whose folio or portfolio association this row describes.
%%field Folio.mutual_fund_scheme_id help: The particular fund, plan and option used by this folio, rather than another similarly named scheme.
%%field Folio.folio_number help: The fund provider's investor reference used to reconcile this scheme holding to external statements.
%%field Folio.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, suspended, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity Portfolio help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective.
%%field Portfolio.id help: The generated key linking this Portfolio record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Portfolio.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field Portfolio.portfolio_name help: The recognizable label for the household's investment grouping, used when choosing the target of advice or execution.
%%field Portfolio.portfolio_type help: The purpose or management arrangement of this investment grouping, used when comparing like portfolios.
%%field Portfolio.base_currency help: The currency in which this plan or portfolio combines monetary values; convert foreign-currency amounts before aggregation.
%%field Portfolio.investment_objective help: The household's stated purpose and constraints for these investments, retained as context for recommendations.
%%field Portfolio.risk_profile_id help: The approved risk context used when assessing this household or portfolio; retain the applicable version for later review.
%%field Portfolio.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, suspended, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity PortfolioAccount help: A dated association of an investment account with a portfolio. Ending the association preserves historical consolidation while changing future reporting.
%%field PortfolioAccount.id help: The generated key linking this PortfolioAccount record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PortfolioAccount.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field PortfolioAccount.investment_account_id help: The provider account whose folio or portfolio association this row describes.
%%field PortfolioAccount.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field PortfolioAccount.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.

%%entity Holding help: Current position of a Security within a Portfolio.
%%field Holding.id help: The generated key linking this Holding record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Holding.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field Holding.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Holding.quantity help: The number of instrument units held, acquired or instructed; retain the product's supported precision and do not treat it as currency.
%%field Holding.average_cost help: The average acquisition cost per unit in the holding's currency, distinguished from the current market price.
%%field Holding.market_value help: The priced value of investments at the relevant valuation date in the portfolio's reporting currency.
%%field Holding.cost_value help: The retained acquisition value in the portfolio's reporting currency, used as the basis for unrealized gain comparison.
%%field Holding.unrealized_gain help: The difference between current market value and retained cost for units still held; it is not a realized cash receipt.
%%field Holding.weight help: The holding's proportion of portfolio value expressed as percent on a 0 to 100 scale.

%%entity HoldingLot help: A separately acquired portion of a holding, retained with acquisition date and cost basis for disposal and tax calculations.
%%field HoldingLot.id help: The generated key linking this HoldingLot record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field HoldingLot.holding_id help: The aggregate investment position affected by this acquisition lot or transaction.
%%field HoldingLot.acquisition_date help: When the units were acquired, used to distinguish acquisition lots for disposal and tax calculations.
%%field HoldingLot.quantity help: The number of instrument units held, acquired or instructed; retain the product's supported precision and do not treat it as currency.
%%field HoldingLot.cost_basis help: The acquisition cost allocated to this lot in its reporting currency; preserve the basis used when computing disposal gains.
%%field HoldingLot.tax_status help: unclassified requires review; taxable, exempt or deferred records the reviewed tax treatment of these acquired units. It does not establish a tax rate or compute a liability.

%%entity PortfolioValuation help: A dated measurement of a portfolio's investments and cash. Net value provides the comparable total for performance and planning calculations.
%%field PortfolioValuation.id help: The generated key linking this PortfolioValuation record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PortfolioValuation.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field PortfolioValuation.valuation_date help: The date the combined investment and cash values describe, used when comparing portfolio history.
%%field PortfolioValuation.market_value help: The priced value of investments at the relevant valuation date in the portfolio's reporting currency.
%%field PortfolioValuation.cost_value help: The retained acquisition value in the portfolio's reporting currency, used as the basis for unrealized gain comparison.
%%field PortfolioValuation.cash_value help: The included uninvested cash in the portfolio's reporting currency at the valuation date.
%%field PortfolioValuation.net_value help: The combined portfolio value after the adjustments included in this valuation; use the same basis across periods.

%%entity AssetAllocationModel help: A target mix of asset classes for a risk category. Its individual targets define acceptable allocation bands rather than actual owned positions.
%%field AssetAllocationModel.id help: The generated key linking this AssetAllocationModel record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AssetAllocationModel.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field AssetAllocationModel.risk_category enum: RiskCategory
%%field AssetAllocationModel.risk_category help: Allowed values are conservative, moderately_conservative, moderate, moderately_aggressive, aggressive. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field AssetAllocationModel.status help: Allowed values are draft, active, superseded, archived. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field AssetAllocationModel.description help: The business explanation of this scenario or allocation model, including which assumptions distinguish it from alternatives.

%%entity AllocationTarget help: The target and permitted lower and upper weights for one asset class within an allocation model. The limits are used when reviewing portfolio drift.
%%field AllocationTarget.id help: The generated key linking this AllocationTarget record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AllocationTarget.asset_allocation_model_id help: The approved target mix used to interpret these weights or the detected allocation drift.
%%field AllocationTarget.asset_class_id help: The investment grouping against which this exposure or performance contribution is measured.
%%field AllocationTarget.target_percentage help: The desired allocation weight on a 0 to 100 scale; compare actual exposure using the same portfolio basis.
%%field AllocationTarget.min_percentage help: The permitted lower allocation weight on a 0 to 100 scale, used to identify underexposure.
%%field AllocationTarget.max_percentage help: The permitted upper allocation weight on a 0 to 100 scale, used to identify excess concentration.

%%entity InvestmentTransaction help: Immutable investment transaction affecting positions, cash or fees.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.id help: The generated key linking this InvestmentTransaction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.holding_id help: The aggregate investment position affected by this acquisition lot or transaction.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.order_id help: The instruction that caused this investment event, providing traceability from approval through execution.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.transaction_type help: The settled or pending investment event, such as acquisition or disposal, that explains how positions or cash are affected.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.transaction_date help: The date the investment event applies to, distinguished from order entry and record-import time.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.quantity help: The number of instrument units held, acquired or instructed; retain the product's supported precision and do not treat it as currency.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.price help: The amount per instrument unit in its quote currency at the observation or transaction date.
%%field InvestmentTransaction.status enum: TransactionStatus
%%field InvestmentTransaction.status help: Allowed values are pending, settled, reversed, failed, cancelled. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity Order help: An instruction to buy, sell or otherwise transact in a security for a client portfolio. Approval, submission and execution are distinct stages.
%%field Order.id help: The generated key linking this Order record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Order.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field Order.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field Order.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Order.order_type help: The investment instruction being issued, such as purchase or sale; check it before interpreting quantity and amount.
%%field Order.status enum: OrderStatus
%%field Order.status help: Allowed values are draft, pending_approval, approved, submitted, partially_executed, executed, rejected, cancelled, failed. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field Order.quantity help: The number of instrument units held, acquired or instructed; retain the product's supported precision and do not treat it as currency.
%%field Order.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field Order.ordered_at help: When the instruction was placed, before any provider acknowledgement or execution is confirmed.
%%field Order.executed_at help: When execution was confirmed; empty means execution has not yet been evidenced.

%%entity SIPInstruction help: A recurring investment instruction specifying an amount, recurrence and funding mandate. The next execution date schedules the next occurrence rather than confirming a completed investment.
%%field SIPInstruction.id help: The generated key linking this SIPInstruction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SIPInstruction.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field SIPInstruction.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field SIPInstruction.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field SIPInstruction.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field SIPInstruction.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field SIPInstruction.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field SIPInstruction.end_date help: The last day the membership, instruction or recurring commitment applies; empty means no scheduled end has been recorded.
%%field SIPInstruction.next_execution_date help: The next scheduled occurrence of the recurring investment; move it only when the scheduling process records a new due date.
%%field SIPInstruction.mandate_reference help: The funding authorisation this recurring investment draws on, as the bank or custodian numbers it. A reference rather than a link: mandates live with the paying bank, not in this model.
%%field SIPInstruction.status help: Allowed values are active, paused, completed, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity InvestmentRecommendation help: Auditable recommendation preserving inputs, risk context, suitability, approval and client decision.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.id help: The generated key linking this InvestmentRecommendation record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.household_id help: The family wealth context used to consolidate this record with related clients, plans and portfolios.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.recommendation_date help: When this advice was prepared against the retained risk and portfolio context.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.recommendation_type help: The purpose of the advice, such as a new allocation or a rebalance, used to understand the intended portfolio change.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.rationale help: The adviser's reasoning for the proposed investments, including relevant client objectives and constraints.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.status enum: RecommendationStatus
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.status help: Allowed values are draft, suitability_check, pending_approval, approved, presented, accepted, executed, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.risk_profile_id help: The approved risk context used when assessing this household or portfolio; retain the applicable version for later review.
%%field InvestmentRecommendation.suitability_status help: Allowed values are pending, passed, failed, requires_review. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity RecommendationItem help: One proposed instrument or allocation within an investment recommendation. Amount, weight and rationale explain its contribution to the proposed portfolio change.
%%field RecommendationItem.id help: The generated key linking this RecommendationItem record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RecommendationItem.investment_recommendation_id help: The advice record whose proposed items, evaluation, review or offer this row belongs to.
%%field RecommendationItem.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field RecommendationItem.asset_class_id help: The investment grouping against which this exposure or performance contribution is measured.
%%field RecommendationItem.recommended_amount help: The proposed investment value in the portfolio's reporting currency, distinguished from an executed trade amount.
%%field RecommendationItem.target_percentage help: The desired allocation weight on a 0 to 100 scale; compare actual exposure using the same portfolio basis.
%%field RecommendationItem.reason help: The explanation for this allocation, assessment change or exception; retain enough context for an adviser to review the decision later.

%%entity SuitabilityResult help: The recorded risk and product-eligibility evaluation of a recommendation. Retain the assessment reference, outcome and evaluation time as approval evidence.
%%field SuitabilityResult.id help: The generated key linking this SuitabilityResult record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SuitabilityResult.investment_recommendation_id help: The advice record whose proposed items, evaluation, review or offer this row belongs to.
%%field SuitabilityResult.assessment_id help: The retained assessment evidence supporting this risk or suitability result; this reference needs an unambiguous model relationship.
%%field SuitabilityResult.result help: The recorded outcome of this assessment or projection, supported by the referenced evidence and explanation.
%%field SuitabilityResult.risk_result help: The recorded outcome of comparing the recommendation with the client's risk context.
%%field SuitabilityResult.eligibility_result help: The recorded outcome of checking whether the client may use the proposed products.
%%field SuitabilityResult.reason help: The explanation for this allocation, assessment change or exception; retain enough context for an adviser to review the decision later.
%%field SuitabilityResult.evaluated_at help: When the recommendation evaluation was recorded; later input changes may require reassessment.

%%entity RecommendationApproval help: A recorded review decision for an investment recommendation. Approver, time and comments evidence authorization rather than implying that execution occurred.
%%field RecommendationApproval.id help: The generated key linking this RecommendationApproval record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RecommendationApproval.investment_recommendation_id help: The advice record whose proposed items, evaluation, review or offer this row belongs to.
%%field RecommendationApproval.approver_id help: The reviewer who made the recommendation decision; confirm the intended reviewer entity before relying on this lookup.
%%field RecommendationApproval.status help: Allowed values are pending, approved, rejected, revoked. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field RecommendationApproval.approved_at help: When the approver's decision was evidenced; empty means no completed approval timestamp is recorded.
%%field RecommendationApproval.comments help: The reviewer's or client's explanation supporting the recorded decision, including exceptions that need follow-up.

%%entity Proposal help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation.
%%field Proposal.id help: The generated key linking this Proposal record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Proposal.investment_recommendation_id help: The advice record whose proposed items, evaluation, review or offer this row belongs to.
%%field Proposal.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field Proposal.proposal_number help: The stable client-facing offer reference, used to distinguish the proposal from the underlying advice record.
%%field Proposal.status enum: ProposalStatus
%%field Proposal.status help: Allowed values are draft, presented, accepted, rejected, expired. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field Proposal.proposal_version help: The business revision of the client-facing offer, distinct from the generator's internal concurrency version.
%%field Proposal.proposal_date help: When this version of the offer was issued to the client.
%%field Proposal.expiry_date help: The date after which this evidence, offer or authority requires renewal; empty means no expiry has been recorded.

%%entity ClientAcceptance help: Retained client decision on a proposal.
%%field ClientAcceptance.id help: The generated key linking this ClientAcceptance record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ClientAcceptance.proposal_id help: The exact client-facing offer whose acceptance or rejection is being retained.
%%field ClientAcceptance.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field ClientAcceptance.decision help: The client's recorded acceptance or rejection of this proposal; retain the associated time and explanation.
%%field ClientAcceptance.decision_at help: When the client made the recorded decision, rather than when the adviser later entered it.
%%field ClientAcceptance.comments help: The reviewer's or client's explanation supporting the recorded decision, including exceptions that need follow-up.

%%entity RebalanceRecommendation help: A proposed correction to portfolio allocation drift. The detected date and explanation retain why the change was raised before trades are authorized.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.id help: The generated key linking this RebalanceRecommendation record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.asset_allocation_model_id help: The approved target mix used to interpret these weights or the detected allocation drift.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.status enum: RebalanceStatus
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.status help: Allowed values are detected, analysed, proposed, approved, executing, completed, failed. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution. Only the transitions drawn in this record's lifecycle are allowed.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.deviation_amount help: The measured allocation drift requiring review; use the same currency or weighting basis as the comparison that detected it.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.detected_date help: When the allocation drift was identified, retained so subsequent review can distinguish old and new observations.
%%field RebalanceRecommendation.reason help: The explanation for this allocation, assessment change or exception; retain enough context for an adviser to review the decision later.

%%entity PerformanceSnapshot help: A dated set of portfolio valuation and return measures. Absolute, money-weighted and time-weighted returns are separate measures and should not be substituted for one another.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.id help: The generated key linking this PerformanceSnapshot record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.portfolio_id help: The investment grouping whose positions, transactions or advice this record concerns; monetary values use its reporting basis.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.snapshot_date help: The date the portfolio value and return observations apply to; compare measures for consistent periods.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.market_value help: The priced value of investments at the relevant valuation date in the portfolio's reporting currency.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.absolute_return help: The total change in investment value expressed as percent for the measured period, without assuming annualization.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.xirr help: The annualized money-weighted return expressed as percent, accounting for dated contributions and withdrawals.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.time_weighted_return help: The return expressed as percent with the effect of external cash-flow timing removed for performance comparison.
%%field PerformanceSnapshot.benchmark_return help: The comparator's return expressed as percent for the same period as the portfolio measurement.

%%entity ClientReview parent: Client
%%entity ClientReview help: A dated adviser review of a client's portfolio, goals and risk context. Recorded recommendations and the next review date support follow-up after the meeting.
%%field ClientReview.status help: due, scheduled, conducted, follow_up, closed describe the review work, independently of the portfolio, goal and risk snapshots.
%%field ClientReview.id help: The generated key linking this ClientReview record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ClientReview.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field ClientReview.review_date help: The planned or actual review date, interpreted in the context of this plan or client-review record.
%%field ClientReview.advisor_id help: The adviser responsible for this work, retained so advice and follow-up can be attributed to the person who provided it.
%%field ClientReview.portfolio_status help: Allowed values are active, inactive, suspended, closed. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field ClientReview.goal_status help: Allowed values are identified, planned, funded, achieved, cancelled. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field ClientReview.risk_status help: Allowed values are draft, assessed, approved, expired, superseded. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field ClientReview.recommendations help: The advice and follow-up recorded during the client review; distinguish it from orders already placed.
%%field ClientReview.next_review_date help: The next planned client review, used to identify relationships requiring follow-up.

%%entity FeeSchedule help: A named basis for charging a fee, including its type, rate and recurrence. A rate must be interpreted using the selected fee basis.
%%field FeeSchedule.id help: The generated key linking this FeeSchedule record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field FeeSchedule.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field FeeSchedule.fee_type help: The charging basis, such as a flat charge or an asset-based percentage, that determines how rate is interpreted.
%%field FeeSchedule.rate help: The agreed fee value on the selected charging basis; record whether it is a percentage or a currency amount consistently.
%%field FeeSchedule.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field FeeSchedule.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity Commission help: Revenue earned in relation to a client and investment product. Earning the amount is distinct from receiving or reconciling it.
%%field Commission.id help: The generated key linking this Commission record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Commission.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field Commission.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Commission.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field Commission.commission_type help: The earning basis used to distinguish upfront revenue from recurring product-related commission.
%%field Commission.earned_date help: When entitlement to this revenue arose, distinct from the date cash was received.
%%field Commission.status help: Allowed values are expected, received, matched, exception, resolved. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.

%%entity CommissionReconciliation help: A comparison of expected commission with the amount received. An exception records a difference requiring investigation rather than silently changing earned revenue.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.id help: The generated key linking this CommissionReconciliation record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.commission_id help: The earned revenue record against which this expected-versus-received comparison is made.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.expected_amount help: The commission amount due in the commission's currency before reconciliation.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.received_amount help: The amount actually received in the same currency; leave empty when receipt has not been confirmed.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.status enum: CommissionStatus
%%field CommissionReconciliation.status help: Allowed values are expected, received, matched, exception, resolved. Record the evidenced outcome; a value does not itself prove approval, verification or execution.
%%field CommissionReconciliation.reconciliation_date help: When expected and received commission were compared, retaining the date of the reconciliation outcome.

%%entity Equity help: Equity-specific information for a security, including trading venue, ticker and economic sector. The associated security carries the common instrument identity.
%%field Equity.id help: The generated key linking this Equity record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Equity.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Equity.exchange help: The venue on which this equity trades, used with ticker to identify the market quote.
%%field Equity.ticker help: The exchange-specific trading shorthand; the same symbol on another venue may refer to another instrument.
%%field Equity.sector help: The issuer's economic grouping used when reviewing concentration in equity exposure.

%%entity Bond help: Debt-instrument terms for a security, including issuer, coupon, maturity and credit assessment. These terms support cash-flow and suitability analysis.
%%field Bond.id help: The generated key linking this Bond record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Bond.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Bond.issuer help: The legal borrower responsible for the debt instrument's contractual payments.
%%field Bond.coupon_rate help: The contractual interest percentage for the debt instrument, interpreted with its payment terms.
%%field Bond.maturity_date help: The contractual date principal falls due or the debt instrument matures; it is not a forecast sale date.
%%field Bond.credit_rating help: The recorded credit assessment for the debt instrument; retain the assessment context when comparing products.

%%entity AIF help: Alternative investment fund details linked to an investable security, including fund classification and the minimum subscription amount.
%%field AIF.id help: The generated key linking this AIF record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AIF.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field AIF.fund_name help: The marketed name of the alternative fund used to match subscription documentation.
%%field AIF.category help: The financial grouping used for this assumption, product or cash flow; apply the same grouping when comparing periods.
%%field AIF.minimum_investment help: The minimum subscription amount in the product's currency; it is a product eligibility input rather than a target allocation.

%%entity PMS help: A portfolio management offering linked to a security, with provider, investment strategy and minimum subscription details.
%%field PMS.id help: The generated key linking this PMS record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PMS.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field PMS.provider_name help: The legal or marketed provider used to match the offering or external service relationship.
%%field PMS.strategy_name help: The portfolio management approach offered by the provider, used to distinguish products with different investment mandates.
%%field PMS.minimum_investment help: The minimum subscription amount in the product's currency; it is a product eligibility input rather than a target allocation.

%%entity Insurance help: Protection-product terms associated with a security, including provider, policy type, premium and insured amount. Protection and investment values should be considered separately.
%%field Insurance.id help: The generated key linking this Insurance record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Insurance.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field Insurance.insurer help: The provider responsible for the insurance contract's protection obligations.
%%field Insurance.policy_type help: The kind of cover offered, used to distinguish protection needs from investment objectives.
%%field Insurance.premium help: The contract's required insurance payment in its currency; interpret the payment interval from the policy terms.
%%field Insurance.sum_assured help: The protection amount payable under the policy conditions, distinct from investment or surrender value.

%%entity RealEstate help: Property-specific information linked to a security, including location and acquisition and current valuation amounts used in wealth consolidation.
%%field RealEstate.id help: The generated key linking this RealEstate record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RealEstate.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field RealEstate.property_type help: The property's use classification, such as residential or commercial, used when reviewing the wealth exposure.
%%field RealEstate.location help: The property's identifiable geographical location used when matching evidence and valuation records.
%%field RealEstate.acquisition_value help: The property's retained purchase valuation in its reporting currency, used as the starting comparison basis.
%%field RealEstate.current_value help: The latest recorded property valuation in the same currency; it is not necessarily an immediately realizable sale price.

%%entity STPInstruction help: A recurring transfer instruction between source and destination investment products for a client. The direction of transfer must remain explicit.
%%field STPInstruction.id help: The generated key linking this STPInstruction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field STPInstruction.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field STPInstruction.source_security_id help: The instrument from which the recurring transfer withdraws value; do not reverse it with the destination.
%%field STPInstruction.target_security_reference help: The instrument receiving the recurring transfer, recorded as its symbol or ISIN. A reference rather than a link: the source security is the one linked security; retain the transfer direction when reviewing instructions.
%%field STPInstruction.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field STPInstruction.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field STPInstruction.status help: Allowed values are active, paused, completed, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity SWPInstruction help: A recurring withdrawal instruction from an investment product. Amount and recurrence describe planned withdrawals rather than completed redemptions.
%%field SWPInstruction.id help: The generated key linking this SWPInstruction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SWPInstruction.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field SWPInstruction.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field SWPInstruction.amount help: The monetary value for this instruction, transaction or planning item in the associated account or planning currency; interpret recurring amounts with frequency.
%%field SWPInstruction.frequency help: The recurrence interval used to annualize cash flows or schedule instructions; the amount is per occurrence.
%%field SWPInstruction.start_date help: The first day the membership, instruction or recurring planning commitment applies; earlier periods are outside its coverage.
%%field SWPInstruction.status help: Allowed values are active, paused, completed, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity CorporateAction help: An issuer event affecting a security, with entitlement and effective dates. Details explain the change that must be reflected in positions or cash.
%%field CorporateAction.id help: The generated key linking this CorporateAction record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field CorporateAction.security_id help: The investable instrument used for this position, price or proposal; verify the product identity before using its values.
%%field CorporateAction.action_type help: The issuer event affecting the instrument, such as a distribution, split or merger, that determines the position treatment.
%%field CorporateAction.record_date help: The issuer's entitlement date used to determine which holders participate in the corporate action.
%%field CorporateAction.effective_date help: The first day the authority, plan or risk context may be relied upon; keep earlier decisions tied to the version then in force.
%%field CorporateAction.status help: Allowed values are announced, pending, applied, cancelled. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field CorporateAction.details help: The terms and evidence needed to understand the issuer event and its effect on positions or cash.

%%entity TaxLot help: The acquisition and cost record used when calculating disposal gains for part of a holding. It retains the tax period independently of the current position.
%%field TaxLot.id help: The generated key linking this TaxLot record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field TaxLot.holding_lot_id help: The separately acquired units whose original cost and acquisition date this tax record preserves.
%%field TaxLot.acquisition_date help: When the units were acquired, used to distinguish acquisition lots for disposal and tax calculations.
%%field TaxLot.quantity help: The number of instrument units held, acquired or instructed; retain the product's supported precision and do not treat it as currency.
%%field TaxLot.cost_basis help: The acquisition cost allocated to this lot in its reporting currency; preserve the basis used when computing disposal gains.
%%field TaxLot.tax_year help: The reporting period under the applicable tax convention; distinguish it from the calendar acquisition date.

%%entity CapitalGain help: A disposal calculation comparing proceeds with the allocated cost basis for a tax lot. Gain type and tax year support later tax reporting.
%%field CapitalGain.id help: The generated key linking this CapitalGain record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field CapitalGain.tax_lot_id help: The acquisition-cost record used to calculate this disposal gain or loss.
%%field CapitalGain.sale_date help: When the units were disposed of, used to allocate the realization to a tax period.
%%field CapitalGain.sale_proceeds help: The disposal consideration allocated to this lot in the calculation currency, on the same gross or net basis used for cost comparison.
%%field CapitalGain.cost_basis help: The acquisition cost allocated to this lot in its reporting currency; preserve the basis used when computing disposal gains.
%%field CapitalGain.gain_amount help: Disposal proceeds less allocated cost basis in the calculation currency; a negative value records a loss.
%%field CapitalGain.gain_type help: The classification of the realization used in the applicable tax calculation; do not infer the applicable tax rate from this label alone.
%%field CapitalGain.tax_year help: The reporting period under the applicable tax convention; distinguish it from the calendar acquisition date.

%%entity Benchmark help: A named reference series used to compare investment performance. Its symbol and type distinguish the relevant comparison market.
%%field Benchmark.id help: The generated key linking this Benchmark record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field Benchmark.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field Benchmark.symbol help: The market or provider shorthand used to locate the investment instrument; distinguish it from a global identifier.
%%field Benchmark.benchmark_type help: The kind of comparison series, such as an index or blended reference, used when selecting a suitable comparator.
%%field Benchmark.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity PerformanceAttribution help: An explanation of an asset class's contribution to a performance snapshot, separating allocation and selection effects where available.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.id help: The generated key linking this PerformanceAttribution record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.performance_snapshot_id help: The dated return observation whose asset-class contribution is being explained.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.asset_class_id help: The investment grouping against which this exposure or performance contribution is measured.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.contribution help: The asset class's contribution to the measured portfolio return, using the attribution calculation's unit consistently.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.allocation_effect help: The part of relative performance attributed to asset-class weighting rather than selection within the class.
%%field PerformanceAttribution.selection_effect help: The part of relative performance attributed to investment selection within the asset class.

%%entity RevenueHierarchy help: An organizational grouping used to organize revenue responsibility. Parent and level retain the reporting hierarchy.
%%field RevenueHierarchy.id help: The generated key linking this RevenueHierarchy record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field RevenueHierarchy.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field RevenueHierarchy.revenue_hierarchy_id help: The revenue grouping immediately above this level; leave empty for a top-level revenue group.
%%field RevenueHierarchy.level_type help: The organizational level represented in the revenue hierarchy, used when aggregating responsibility.
%%field RevenueHierarchy.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity SubBroker help: A distribution intermediary identified by a business code and linked party. Status controls whether the relationship is current.
%%field SubBroker.id help: The generated key linking this SubBroker record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field SubBroker.party_id help: The legal identity this record belongs to; linking the existing party preserves a single identity across household and client roles.
%%field SubBroker.code help: The intermediary's stable business reference used when reconciling distribution relationships.
%%field SubBroker.name help: The business-readable label used to select this record in planning and advisory work; distinguish records with similar purposes.
%%field SubBroker.status help: Allowed values are active, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.

%%entity AdvancedComplianceRecord help: A dated compliance review for a client, retaining the review type, outcome and lifecycle independently of identification evidence.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.id help: The generated key linking this AdvancedComplianceRecord record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.client_id help: The client relationship whose instructions, evidence or investment activity this record concerns.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.compliance_type help: The regulatory or policy review being recorded, used to distinguish its evidence from routine client identification.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.status help: Allowed values are pending, in_review, compliant, non_compliant, resolved, expired. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.review_date help: The planned or actual review date, interpreted in the context of this plan or client-review record.
%%field AdvancedComplianceRecord.result help: The recorded outcome of this assessment or projection, supported by the referenced evidence and explanation.

%%entity ExternalIntegration help: A configured external-system relationship with a provider and endpoint. The last synchronization time records completed exchange, not a promise of freshness.
%%field ExternalIntegration.id help: The generated key linking this ExternalIntegration record to its related wealth-management evidence; retain it when reconciling imports or references.
%%field ExternalIntegration.integration_type help: The business exchange served by this connection, such as account reconciliation or product data refresh.
%%field ExternalIntegration.provider_name help: The legal or marketed provider used to match the offering or external service relationship.
%%field ExternalIntegration.endpoint_url help: The configured provider endpoint for this exchange; a stored address does not itself implement authentication or synchronization.
%%field ExternalIntegration.status help: Allowed values are active, paused, failed, inactive. Record the evidenced business classification or outcome; changing this field does not itself complete the underlying work.
%%field ExternalIntegration.last_sync_at help: When a completed exchange was last recorded, used when judging whether imported account information needs refresh.

    %% Form layout: headed sections of two-column rows (`|` between rows,
    %% `,` within one; a row of one spans the full width).
    %%section entity: Party; name: Party; help: Anyone the firm deals with — a person or an organisation — under the name every screen shows.; rows: display_name, party_type | status
    %%section entity: Person; name: Name; help: The person's legal name, as identity documents and KYC checks must match it.; rows: first_name, middle_name | last_name, party_id
    %%section entity: Person; name: Profile; help: The personal facts suitability and tax residency are judged on.; rows: date_of_birth, gender | marital_status, nationality | occupation
    %%section entity: Organization; name: Organisation; help: The legal entity as its registration documents name it, and the identifiers tax and KYC checks use.; rows: legal_name, organization_type | registration_number, tax_identifier | party_id
    %%section entity: Household; name: Household; help: The family or group advised together, the advisor who leads it, and whether it is still a client.; rows: name, status | primary_advisor_id, relationship_manager_reference
    %%section entity: Household; name: Wealth and risk; help: What the household earns, what it is worth, and the risk profile its plans must respect.; rows: annual_income, net_worth | risk_profile_id
    %%section entity: HouseholdMember; name: Membership; help: Who belongs to the household, how they are related, and their share of what it owns.; rows: household_id, party_id | relationship_type, ownership_percentage | is_primary
    %%section entity: HouseholdMember; name: Period; help: When the person joined the household and, if they have left it, when.; rows: start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Client; name: Client; help: The party as a client of the firm — the number they are known by, the household they sit in, and where the relationship stands.; rows: client_number | party_id, household_id | client_type, onboarding_date
    %%section entity: Client; name: Service; help: Who advises the client, the service they receive, and how they are charged for it.; rows: advisor_id, service_model | fee_model
    %%section entity: Address; name: Address; help: One address a party uses and what it is for — the primary one is where statements go.; rows: party_id, address_type | line1 | city, region | postal_code, country | is_primary
    %%section entity: ContactPoint; name: Contact point; help: One way to reach a party, whether it is the default, and whether it has been proven to reach them.; rows: party_id, contact_type | value | is_primary, verified
    %%section entity: Nominee; name: Nomination; help: Who receives a share of the client's holdings on death, and how large that share is.; rows: client_id, nominee_party_id | relationship_type, allocation_percentage
    %%section entity: Nominee; name: Period; help: When the nomination took effect and when it was revoked, if it was.; rows: start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: PowerOfAttorney; name: Authority; help: Who granted authority to act for them, to whom, and what it covers.; rows: grantor_party_id, attorney_party_reference | status | scope
    %%section entity: PowerOfAttorney; name: Validity; help: When the power took effect and when it lapses — instructions outside these dates are refused.; rows: effective_date, expiry_date
    %%section entity: OrganizationUnit; name: Unit; help: A branch, region or desk of the firm and the unit it reports into.; rows: name, unit_type | organization_unit_id, status
    %%section entity: Advisor; name: Advisor; help: The person who advises clients, the unit they work in, and whether they can take new households.; rows: party_id, employee_number | organization_unit_id, advisor_type | status
    %%section entity: Advisor; name: Licence; help: The regulatory licence that allows them to advise, and when it must be renewed.; rows: license_number, license_expiry
    %%section entity: AdvisorAssignment; name: Assignment; help: Which advisor serves which household, in what capacity, and whether they lead it.; rows: advisor_id, household_id | assignment_type, is_primary | start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Team; name: Team; help: A group of advisors working together, the unit it belongs to, and what kind of work it does.; rows: name, team_type | organization_unit_id, status
    %%section entity: TeamMember; name: Membership; help: Which advisor is on which team, in what role, and for how long.; rows: team_id, advisor_id | role | start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Prospect; name: Prospect; help: A party who may become a client, where they came from, and the advisor pursuing them.; rows: party_id | source, assigned_advisor_id
    %%section entity: Prospect; name: Potential; help: How promising the prospect looks, what they might bring, and when the next step is due.; rows: lead_score, estimated_aum | next_action_date
    %%section entity: Interaction; name: Interaction; help: One conversation or meeting with a party — who, when, how, and what was discussed.; rows: party_id, advisor_id | interaction_type, interaction_at | subject | notes
    %%section entity: Activity; name: Activity; help: A task for a client's advisor, how urgent it is, and when it must be done.; rows: subject | client_id, advisor_id | activity_type, priority | due_date, status | completed_at
    %%section entity: ServiceRequest; name: Request; help: Something the client asked the firm to do and where it stands.; rows: subject | client_id, request_type | priority | submitted_at, completed_at
    %%section entity: OnboardingCase; name: Onboarding; help: The process of turning a prospect into a client — who runs it and how far it has got.; rows: client_id, prospect_id | status, assigned_advisor_id | started_date, completed_date
    %%section entity: KYCRecord; name: KYC; help: The client's know-your-customer standing — no account may be opened or traded without a current one.; rows: client_id, kyc_status | kyc_type, kyc_identifier
    %%section entity: KYCRecord; name: Verification; help: When identity was last verified, against what source, and when it must be done again.; rows: verification_date, verification_source | expiry_date
    %%section entity: KYCVerification; name: Check; help: One identity check performed for the KYC record and its outcome.; rows: kyc_record_id, verification_type | status, verified_at | verification_source, reference_number
    %%section entity: FATCADeclaration; name: Declaration; help: The client's US tax status, which decides whether their accounts are reported to the IRS.; rows: client_id, us_person | tax_residency, country | tin, declaration_date
    %%section entity: CRSDeclaration; name: Declaration; help: Where the client is tax resident, which decides which countries their accounts are reported to.; rows: client_id, status | tax_residency, country | tin, declaration_date
    %%section entity: SuitabilityAssessment; name: Assessment; help: The test of what investments suit the client, who ran it, and what it concluded.; rows: client_id, assessor_id | assessment_type, assessment_date | status, result
    %%section entity: IdentityDocument; name: Document; help: A passport, ID card or similar the party has supplied, and whether it has been verified.; rows: party_id, document_type | document_number, verification_status | issue_date, expiry_date
    %%section entity: ESignatureRequest; name: Signature request; help: A document sent to the client for electronic signature and where it stands with the provider.; rows: client_id, document_id | status, provider_reference | requested_at, signed_at
    %%section entity: BankAccount; name: Bank account; help: An account the client pays from and is paid into, and whether it is the default.; rows: client_id, is_primary | bank_name, account_type | account_number, verification_status
    %%section entity: BankAccount; name: Branch; help: The branch that holds the account and the code payments are routed by.; rows: branch, ifsc
    %%section entity: Document; name: Document; help: A file held about a party, what kind it is, and when it was received.; rows: party_id, document_type | file_name, status | document_url | uploaded_at
    %%section entity: AuditEvent; name: Event; help: What was done, by whom, when, and from where — the record a regulator asks for.; rows: timestamp, action | user_reference, source | ip_address, correlation_reference
    %%section entity: AuditEvent; name: Change; help: The record that was changed and its value before and after.; rows: entity_type, entity_reference | before_value | after_value
    %%section entity: FinancialPlan; name: Plan; help: The household's financial plan, which version is in force, and who prepared it.; rows: plan_number, plan_version | household_id, advisor_id | base_currency
    %%section entity: FinancialPlan; name: Dates; help: When the plan took effect and when it is next reviewed.; rows: effective_date, review_date
    %%section entity: FinancialPlanAssumption; name: Assumption; help: One figure the plan's projections rest on — inflation, a return, a retirement age — and where it came from.; rows: financial_plan_id, assumption_type | value, unit | source
    %%section entity: IncomeSource; name: Income; help: Money coming into the household that the plan counts on — whose, what kind, and how much.; rows: financial_plan_id, party_id | income_type, amount | frequency, inflation_linked
    %%section entity: IncomeSource; name: Period; help: When the income starts and stops; a pension starts on the day it is first paid.; rows: start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Expense; name: Expense; help: Money the household spends that the plan must fund, and whether it rises with inflation.; rows: financial_plan_id, expense_type | amount, frequency | inflation_linked
    %%section entity: Expense; name: Period; help: When the expense begins and ends — school fees stop when the youngest leaves.; rows: start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Liability; name: Liability; help: A debt the household owes, how much is left, and what it costs.; rows: financial_plan_id, liability_type | outstanding_amount, interest_rate | monthly_payment, status | maturity_date
    %%section entity: CashFlow; name: Cash flow; help: One projected flow of money in the plan, what it is for, and how often it recurs.; rows: financial_plan_id, cashflow_type | category, amount | frequency, inflation_linked
    %%section entity: CashFlow; name: Period; help: The years the flow runs between.; rows: start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Goal; name: Goal; help: Something the household is saving towards, which plan funds it, and how important it is.; rows: name, goal_type | household_id, financial_plan_id | priority
    %%section entity: Goal; name: Target; help: How much is needed, by when, and how much of it is already covered.; rows: target_amount, target_date | funded_percentage
    %%section entity: GoalFunding; name: Funding; help: What is set aside for a goal — a holding, a portfolio or a cash flow — and how much of it.; rows: goal_id, allocated_amount | portfolio_id, security_id | cashflow_id
    %%section entity: GoalProjection; name: Projection; help: What a scenario expects the goal to be worth on a date, and the shortfall if it falls short.; rows: goal_id, scenario_id | projection_date, result | projected_value, shortfall
    %%section entity: Scenario; name: Scenario; help: A what-if the plan is tested against, and whether it is the one presented to the household.; rows: name, scenario_type | financial_plan_id, status | description
    %%section entity: ScenarioAssumption; name: Assumption; help: One figure the scenario changes from the plan's base assumptions.; rows: scenario_id, assumption_type | value, unit
    %%section entity: RiskAssessment; name: Assessment; help: The questionnaire that measures how much risk the client can bear, and what it found.; rows: client_id, household_id | assessment_type, assessment_date | status, result
    %%section entity: RiskProfile; name: Profile; help: The risk category investments must stay within, and the assessment it was set from.; rows: client_id, household_id | risk_score, risk_category | assessment_id, status
    %%section entity: RiskProfile; name: Validity; help: When the profile took effect and when it must be reassessed.; rows: effective_date, expiry_date
    %%section entity: RiskProfileHistory; name: Change; help: An earlier risk profile and why it was replaced — what a suitability review looks back on.; rows: risk_profile_id | risk_score, risk_category | effective_date, expiry_date | reason
    %%section entity: Security; name: Security; help: An instrument that can be held or traded, the ticker and ISIN it is identified by, and whether it can still be bought.; rows: name, symbol | isin, security_type_id | currency, status
    %%section entity: SecurityType; name: Type; help: A kind of instrument and the category it reports under.; rows: name, category | status
    %%section entity: MutualFundScheme; name: Scheme; help: The fund scheme, the house that runs it, and the codes it is ordered by.; rows: scheme_name, scheme_code | security_id, amc_id | isin
    %%section entity: MutualFundScheme; name: Classification; help: What kind of fund it is, which plan and option, and the benchmark and risk it is measured against.; rows: category, risk_level | plan_type, option_type | benchmark
    %%section entity: AMC; name: Asset manager; help: The fund house, its regulatory registration, and whether its schemes can be sold.; rows: name, registration_number | status
    %%section entity: ProductPrice; name: Price; help: A security's price on a date, what kind of price it is, and where it was sourced.; rows: security_id, price_date | price, price_type | source
    %%section entity: AssetClass; name: Asset class; help: A class of asset allocation targets are set against, and the broader class it falls under.; rows: name, asset_class_id | status
    %%section entity: InvestmentAccount; name: Account; help: An account the client holds investments in, at which institution, and how it is owned.; rows: account_number, status | client_id, institution_id | account_type, ownership_type | opened_date
    %%section entity: Folio; name: Folio; help: The folio number a fund house holds the client's units in for one scheme.; rows: folio_number, status | investment_account_id, mutual_fund_scheme_id
    %%section entity: Portfolio; name: Portfolio; help: A managed set of holdings for the household, what it is for, and the risk profile it must respect.; rows: portfolio_name, status | household_id, portfolio_type | risk_profile_id, base_currency | investment_objective
    %%section entity: PortfolioAccount; name: Account in portfolio; help: Which investment account is managed as part of the portfolio, and for how long.; rows: portfolio_id, investment_account_id | start_date, end_date
    %%section entity: Holding; name: Holding; help: A position in one security within a portfolio and how much of it is held.; rows: portfolio_id, security_id | quantity, weight
    %%section entity: Holding; name: Value; help: What the position cost, what it is worth now, and the gain not yet realised.; rows: average_cost, cost_value | market_value, unrealized_gain
    %%section entity: HoldingLot; name: Lot; help: One purchase that makes up a holding — when, how much, at what cost, and how its gain is taxed.; rows: holding_id, acquisition_date | quantity, cost_basis | tax_status
    %%section entity: PortfolioValuation; name: Valuation; help: What the portfolio was worth on a date, split between invested and cash.; rows: portfolio_id, valuation_date | market_value, cost_value | cash_value, net_value
    %%section entity: AssetAllocationModel; name: Model; help: A target mix of asset classes for one risk category, which portfolios are rebalanced towards.; rows: name, risk_category | status | description
    %%section entity: AllocationTarget; name: Target; help: The share of one asset class in the model and the band it may drift within before rebalancing.; rows: asset_allocation_model_id, asset_class_id | target_percentage | min_percentage, max_percentage
    %%section entity: InvestmentTransaction; name: Transaction; help: A completed trade or corporate action against a holding, and the order it came from.; rows: transaction_type, status | portfolio_id, holding_id | order_id, transaction_date
    %%section entity: InvestmentTransaction; name: Amount; help: How many units moved, at what price, and for what total.; rows: quantity, price | amount
