%%report financial-plan-lifecycle title: Financial Plan lifecycle entity: FinancialPlan chart: bar x: state y: records help: Versioned household financial plan describing objectives, assumptions, scenarios and funding requirements. Where financial plans sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'analysis', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'proposed', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'superseded', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'archived', 6) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report financial-plan-top-base-currency title: Financial Plans: the most common base currency entity: FinancialPlan chart: bar x: base_currency y: records help: Versioned household financial plan describing objectives, assumptions, scenarios and funding requirements. The ten most frequent values of base currency among financial plans; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(base_currency, '(blank)') AS base_currency, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_plan WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report financial-plan-assumption-per-financial-plan title: Financial Plan Assumptions per financial plan entity: FinancialPlanAssumption chart: bar x: financial_plan y: records help: One assumption underlying a financial plan, retained with its value, unit and source so projections can be reviewed and reproduced. Which financial plan the most financial plan assumptions belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.plan_number::text, '(none)') AS financial_plan, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_plan_assumption x LEFT JOIN bus_financial_plan p ON p.id = x.financial_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report financial-plan-assumption-top-unit title: Financial Plan Assumptions: the most common unit entity: FinancialPlanAssumption chart: bar x: unit y: records help: One assumption underlying a financial plan, retained with its value, unit and source so projections can be reviewed and reproduced. The ten most frequent values of unit among financial plan assumptions; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(unit, '(blank)') AS unit, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_plan_assumption WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report financial-plan-assumption-top-source title: Financial Plan Assumptions: the most common source entity: FinancialPlanAssumption chart: bar x: source y: records help: One assumption underlying a financial plan, retained with its value, unit and source so projections can be reviewed and reproduced. The ten most frequent values of source among financial plan assumptions; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(source, '(blank)') AS source, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_financial_plan_assumption WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report income-source-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month entity: IncomeSource chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: A dated stream of household income used in a plan. The average amount of income sources created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_income_source WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report income-source-largest-by-amount title: The ten largest income sources by amount entity: IncomeSource chart: bar x: record y: amount help: A dated stream of household income used in a plan. The records with the highest amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT income_type::text AS record, amount FROM bus_income_source WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report income-source-per-financial-plan title: Income Sources per financial plan entity: IncomeSource chart: bar x: financial_plan y: records help: A dated stream of household income used in a plan. Which financial plan the most income sources belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.plan_number::text, '(none)') AS financial_plan, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_income_source x LEFT JOIN bus_financial_plan p ON p.id = x.financial_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
