%%report expense-largest-by-amount title: The ten largest expenses by amount entity: Expense chart: bar x: record y: amount help: A planned outflow with a recurrence and effective period. The records with the highest amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT expense_type::text AS record, amount FROM bus_expense WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report expense-per-financial-plan title: Expenses per financial plan entity: Expense chart: bar x: financial_plan y: records help: A planned outflow with a recurrence and effective period. Which financial plan the most expenses belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.plan_number::text, '(none)') AS financial_plan, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_expense x LEFT JOIN bus_financial_plan p ON p.id = x.financial_plan_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report liability-by-status title: Liabilities by status entity: Liability chart: pie x: status y: records help: A debt included in the household plan, carrying outstanding principal, borrowing cost and repayment timing. How liabilities divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_liability WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report liability-outstanding-amount-by-status title: Total outstanding amount by status entity: Liability chart: bar x: status y: total_outstanding_amount help: A debt included in the household plan, carrying outstanding principal, borrowing cost and repayment timing. Liabilities added up on outstanding amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(outstanding_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_outstanding_amount FROM bus_liability WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report liability-outstanding-amount-per-month title: Average outstanding amount per month entity: Liability chart: line x: month y: average_outstanding_amount help: A debt included in the household plan, carrying outstanding principal, borrowing cost and repayment timing. The average outstanding amount of liabilities created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(outstanding_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_outstanding_amount FROM bus_liability WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report cash-flow-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (Cash Flow) entity: CashFlow chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: A dated inflow or outflow used in planning calculations. The average amount of cash flows created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_cash_flow WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
