%%report asset-class-by-status title: Asset Classes by status entity: AssetClass chart: pie x: status y: records help: A grouping used to set allocation targets and compare exposure. How asset classes divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_class WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report asset-class-created-per-month title: Asset Classes created per month entity: AssetClass chart: line x: month y: records help: A grouping used to set allocation targets and compare exposure. New asset classes per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_class WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report asset-class-per-asset-class title: Asset Classes per asset class entity: AssetClass chart: bar x: asset_class y: records help: A grouping used to set allocation targets and compare exposure. Which asset class the most asset classes belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS asset_class, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_class x LEFT JOIN bus_asset_class p ON p.id = x.asset_class_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report investment-account-by-status title: Investment Accounts by status entity: InvestmentAccount chart: pie x: status y: records help: A client account held with an investment institution. How investment accounts divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report investment-account-top-account-type title: Investment Accounts: the most common account type entity: InvestmentAccount chart: bar x: account_type y: records help: A client account held with an investment institution. The ten most frequent values of account type among investment accounts; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(account_type, '(blank)') AS account_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report investment-account-top-ownership-type title: Investment Accounts: the most common ownership type entity: InvestmentAccount chart: bar x: ownership_type y: records help: A client account held with an investment institution. The ten most frequent values of ownership type among investment accounts; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(ownership_type, '(blank)') AS ownership_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report folio-by-status title: Folios by status entity: Folio chart: pie x: status y: records help: A mutual fund investor reference associated with an investment account and scheme. How folios divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_folio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report folio-per-investment-account title: Folios per investment account entity: Folio chart: bar x: investment_account y: records help: A mutual fund investor reference associated with an investment account and scheme. Which investment account the most folios belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.account_number::text, '(none)') AS investment_account, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_folio x LEFT JOIN bus_investment_account p ON p.id = x.investment_account_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report folio-per-mutual-fund-scheme title: Folios per mutual fund scheme entity: Folio chart: bar x: mutual_fund_scheme y: records help: A mutual fund investor reference associated with an investment account and scheme. Which mutual fund scheme the most folios belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.scheme_code::text, '(none)') AS mutual_fund_scheme, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_folio x LEFT JOIN bus_mutual_fund_scheme p ON p.id = x.mutual_fund_scheme_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report portfolio-by-status title: Portfolios by status entity: Portfolio chart: pie x: status y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. How portfolios divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report portfolio-created-per-month title: Portfolios created per month entity: Portfolio chart: line x: month y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. New portfolios per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report portfolio-created-by-weekday title: Portfolios created by day of the week entity: Portfolio chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. Which days portfolios are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report portfolio-age-bands title: How recently portfolios were changed entity: Portfolio chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report portfolio-top-portfolio-type title: Portfolios: the most common portfolio type entity: Portfolio chart: bar x: portfolio_type y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. The ten most frequent values of portfolio type among portfolios; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(portfolio_type, '(blank)') AS portfolio_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report portfolio-top-base-currency title: Portfolios: the most common base currency entity: Portfolio chart: bar x: base_currency y: records help: Logical investment portfolio representing actual owned wealth and its investment objective. The ten most frequent values of base currency among portfolios; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(base_currency, '(blank)') AS base_currency, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report portfolio-account-created-per-month title: Portfolio Accounts created per month entity: PortfolioAccount chart: line x: month y: records help: A dated association of an investment account with a portfolio. New portfolio accounts per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report portfolio-account-per-portfolio title: Portfolio Accounts per portfolio entity: PortfolioAccount chart: bar x: portfolio y: records help: A dated association of an investment account with a portfolio. Which portfolio the most portfolio accounts belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.portfolio_name::text, '(none)') AS portfolio, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio_account x LEFT JOIN bus_portfolio p ON p.id = x.portfolio_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report portfolio-account-per-investment-account title: Portfolio Accounts per investment account entity: PortfolioAccount chart: bar x: investment_account y: records help: A dated association of an investment account with a portfolio. Which investment account the most portfolio accounts belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.account_number::text, '(none)') AS investment_account, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_portfolio_account x LEFT JOIN bus_investment_account p ON p.id = x.investment_account_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report holding-average-cost-per-month title: Average average cost per month entity: Holding chart: line x: month y: average_average_cost help: Current position of a Security within a Portfolio. The average average cost of holdings created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(average_cost)::numeric, 2) AS average_average_cost FROM bus_holding WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report holding-largest-by-average-cost title: The ten largest holdings by average cost entity: Holding chart: bar x: record y: average_cost help: Current position of a Security within a Portfolio. The records with the highest average cost; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT quantity::text AS record, average_cost FROM bus_holding WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND average_cost IS NOT NULL ORDER BY average_cost DESC LIMIT 10
%%report holding-market-value-per-month title: Average market value per month entity: Holding chart: line x: month y: average_market_value help: Current position of a Security within a Portfolio. The average market value of holdings created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(market_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_market_value FROM bus_holding WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report holding-lot-by-tax-status title: Holding Lots by tax status entity: HoldingLot chart: pie x: tax_status y: records help: A separately acquired portion of a holding, retained with acquisition date and cost basis for disposal and tax calculations. How holding lots divide across tax status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(tax_status::text, '(unset)') AS tax_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_holding_lot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report holding-lot-cost-basis-by-tax-status title: Total cost basis by tax status entity: HoldingLot chart: bar x: tax_status y: total_cost_basis help: A separately acquired portion of a holding, retained with acquisition date and cost basis for disposal and tax calculations. Holding Lots added up on cost basis, split by tax status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(tax_status::text, '(unset)') AS tax_status, ROUND(SUM(cost_basis)::numeric, 2) AS total_cost_basis FROM bus_holding_lot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report holding-lot-cost-basis-per-month title: Average cost basis per month entity: HoldingLot chart: line x: month y: average_cost_basis help: A separately acquired portion of a holding, retained with acquisition date and cost basis for disposal and tax calculations. The average cost basis of holding lots created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(cost_basis)::numeric, 2) AS average_cost_basis FROM bus_holding_lot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report portfolio-valuation-market-value-per-month title: Average market value per month (Portfolio Valuation) entity: PortfolioValuation chart: line x: month y: average_market_value help: A dated measurement of a portfolio's investments and cash. The average market value of portfolio valuations created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(market_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_market_value FROM bus_portfolio_valuation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report portfolio-valuation-cost-value-per-month title: Average cost value per month (Portfolio Valuation) entity: PortfolioValuation chart: line x: month y: average_cost_value help: A dated measurement of a portfolio's investments and cash. The average cost value of portfolio valuations created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(cost_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_cost_value FROM bus_portfolio_valuation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report portfolio-valuation-cash-value-per-month title: Average cash value per month entity: PortfolioValuation chart: line x: month y: average_cash_value help: A dated measurement of a portfolio's investments and cash. The average cash value of portfolio valuations created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(cash_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_cash_value FROM bus_portfolio_valuation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report asset-allocation-model-by-status title: Asset Allocation Models by status entity: AssetAllocationModel chart: pie x: status y: records help: A target mix of asset classes for a risk category. How asset allocation models divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_allocation_model WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report asset-allocation-model-by-risk-category title: Asset Allocation Models by risk category entity: AssetAllocationModel chart: pie x: risk_category y: records help: A target mix of asset classes for a risk category. How asset allocation models divide across risk category, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(risk_category::text, '(unset)') AS risk_category, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_allocation_model WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report asset-allocation-model-created-per-month title: Asset Allocation Models created per month entity: AssetAllocationModel chart: line x: month y: records help: A target mix of asset classes for a risk category. New asset allocation models per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_asset_allocation_model WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report allocation-target-target-percentage-per-month title: Average target percentage per month entity: AllocationTarget chart: line x: month y: average_target_percentage help: The target and permitted lower and upper weights for one asset class within an allocation model. The average target percentage of allocation targets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(target_percentage)::numeric, 2) AS average_target_percentage FROM bus_allocation_target WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report allocation-target-min-percentage-per-month title: Average min percentage per month entity: AllocationTarget chart: line x: month y: average_min_percentage help: The target and permitted lower and upper weights for one asset class within an allocation model. The average min percentage of allocation targets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(min_percentage)::numeric, 2) AS average_min_percentage FROM bus_allocation_target WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report allocation-target-max-percentage-per-month title: Average max percentage per month entity: AllocationTarget chart: line x: month y: average_max_percentage help: The target and permitted lower and upper weights for one asset class within an allocation model. The average max percentage of allocation targets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(max_percentage)::numeric, 2) AS average_max_percentage FROM bus_allocation_target WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report investment-transaction-by-status title: Investment Transactions by status entity: InvestmentTransaction chart: pie x: status y: records help: Immutable investment transaction affecting positions, cash or fees. How investment transactions divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report investment-transaction-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status entity: InvestmentTransaction chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: Immutable investment transaction affecting positions, cash or fees. Investment Transactions added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_investment_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report investment-transaction-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (Investment Transaction) entity: InvestmentTransaction chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: Immutable investment transaction affecting positions, cash or fees. The average amount of investment transactions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_investment_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report order-by-status title: Orders by status entity: Order chart: bar x: status y: records help: An instruction to buy, sell or otherwise transact in a security for a client portfolio. How orders divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report order-lifecycle title: Order lifecycle entity: Order chart: bar x: state y: records help: An instruction to buy, sell or otherwise transact in a security for a client portfolio. Where orders sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'pending_approval', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'submitted', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'partially_executed', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'executed', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'rejected', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 7 UNION ALL SELECT 'failed', 8) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report order-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status (Order) entity: Order chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: An instruction to buy, sell or otherwise transact in a security for a client portfolio. Orders added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report sip-instruction-by-status title: SIPInstructions by status entity: SIPInstruction chart: pie x: status y: records help: A recurring investment instruction specifying an amount, recurrence and funding mandate. How sipinstructions divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_sip_instruction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report sip-instruction-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status (SIPInstruction) entity: SIPInstruction chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: A recurring investment instruction specifying an amount, recurrence and funding mandate. SIPInstructions added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_sip_instruction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report sip-instruction-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (SIPInstruction) entity: SIPInstruction chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: A recurring investment instruction specifying an amount, recurrence and funding mandate. The average amount of sipinstructions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_sip_instruction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report investment-recommendation-by-status title: Investment Recommendations by status entity: InvestmentRecommendation chart: bar x: status y: records help: Auditable recommendation preserving inputs, risk context, suitability, approval and client decision. How investment recommendations divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report investment-recommendation-by-suitability-status title: Investment Recommendations by suitability status entity: InvestmentRecommendation chart: pie x: suitability_status y: records help: Auditable recommendation preserving inputs, risk context, suitability, approval and client decision. How investment recommendations divide across suitability status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(suitability_status::text, '(unset)') AS suitability_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report investment-recommendation-lifecycle title: Investment Recommendation lifecycle entity: InvestmentRecommendation chart: bar x: state y: records help: Auditable recommendation preserving inputs, risk context, suitability, approval and client decision. Where investment recommendations sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'suitability_check', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'pending_approval', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'presented', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'accepted', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'executed', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'rejected', 7 UNION ALL SELECT 'expired', 8) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_investment_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report recommendation-item-recommended-amount-per-month title: Average recommended amount per month entity: RecommendationItem chart: line x: month y: average_recommended_amount help: One proposed instrument or allocation within an investment recommendation. The average recommended amount of recommendation items created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(recommended_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_recommended_amount FROM bus_recommendation_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report recommendation-item-largest-by-recommended-amount title: The ten largest recommendation items by recommended amount entity: RecommendationItem chart: bar x: record y: recommended_amount help: One proposed instrument or allocation within an investment recommendation. The records with the highest recommended amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT reason::text AS record, recommended_amount FROM bus_recommendation_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND recommended_amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY recommended_amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report recommendation-item-target-percentage-per-month title: Average target percentage per month (Recommendation Item) entity: RecommendationItem chart: line x: month y: average_target_percentage help: One proposed instrument or allocation within an investment recommendation. The average target percentage of recommendation items created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(target_percentage)::numeric, 2) AS average_target_percentage FROM bus_recommendation_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report suitability-result-per-investment-recommendation title: Suitability Results per investment recommendation entity: SuitabilityResult chart: bar x: investment_recommendation y: records help: The recorded risk and product-eligibility evaluation of a recommendation. Which investment recommendation the most suitability results belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.recommendation_type::text, '(none)') AS investment_recommendation, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_suitability_result x LEFT JOIN bus_investment_recommendation p ON p.id = x.investment_recommendation_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report suitability-result-top-risk-result title: Suitability Results: the most common risk result entity: SuitabilityResult chart: bar x: risk_result y: records help: The recorded risk and product-eligibility evaluation of a recommendation. The ten most frequent values of risk result among suitability results; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(risk_result, '(blank)') AS risk_result, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_suitability_result WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report suitability-result-top-eligibility-result title: Suitability Results: the most common eligibility result entity: SuitabilityResult chart: bar x: eligibility_result y: records help: The recorded risk and product-eligibility evaluation of a recommendation. The ten most frequent values of eligibility result among suitability results; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(eligibility_result, '(blank)') AS eligibility_result, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_suitability_result WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report recommendation-approval-by-status title: Recommendation Approvals by status entity: RecommendationApproval chart: pie x: status y: records help: A recorded review decision for an investment recommendation. How recommendation approvals divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_recommendation_approval WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report recommendation-approval-created-per-month title: Recommendation Approvals created per month entity: RecommendationApproval chart: line x: month y: records help: A recorded review decision for an investment recommendation. New recommendation approvals per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_recommendation_approval WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report recommendation-approval-per-investment-recommendation title: Recommendation Approvals per investment recommendation entity: RecommendationApproval chart: bar x: investment_recommendation y: records help: A recorded review decision for an investment recommendation. Which investment recommendation the most recommendation approvals belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.recommendation_type::text, '(none)') AS investment_recommendation, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_recommendation_approval x LEFT JOIN bus_investment_recommendation p ON p.id = x.investment_recommendation_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report proposal-by-status title: Proposals by status entity: Proposal chart: pie x: status y: records help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation. How proposals divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_proposal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report proposal-lifecycle title: Proposal lifecycle entity: Proposal chart: bar x: state y: records help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation. Where proposals sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'presented', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'accepted', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'rejected', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'expired', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_proposal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report proposal-created-per-month title: Proposals created per month entity: Proposal chart: line x: month y: records help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation. New proposals per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_proposal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report proposal-per-investment-recommendation title: Proposals per investment recommendation entity: Proposal chart: bar x: investment_recommendation y: records help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation. Which investment recommendation the most proposals belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.recommendation_type::text, '(none)') AS investment_recommendation, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_proposal x LEFT JOIN bus_investment_recommendation p ON p.id = x.investment_recommendation_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report proposal-per-client title: Proposals per client entity: Proposal chart: bar x: client y: records help: Client-facing proposal generated from an approved recommendation. Which client the most proposals belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.client_number::text, '(none)') AS client, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_proposal x LEFT JOIN bus_client p ON p.id = x.client_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report client-acceptance-created-per-month title: Client Acceptances created per month entity: ClientAcceptance chart: line x: month y: records help: Retained client decision on a proposal. New client acceptances per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_acceptance WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report client-acceptance-per-proposal title: Client Acceptances per proposal entity: ClientAcceptance chart: bar x: proposal y: records help: Retained client decision on a proposal. Which proposal the most client acceptances belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.proposal_number::text, '(none)') AS proposal, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_acceptance x LEFT JOIN bus_proposal p ON p.id = x.proposal_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report client-acceptance-per-client title: Client Acceptances per client entity: ClientAcceptance chart: bar x: client y: records help: Retained client decision on a proposal. Which client the most client acceptances belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.client_number::text, '(none)') AS client, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_acceptance x LEFT JOIN bus_client p ON p.id = x.client_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report rebalance-recommendation-by-status title: Rebalance Recommendations by status entity: RebalanceRecommendation chart: bar x: status y: records help: A proposed correction to portfolio allocation drift. How rebalance recommendations divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rebalance_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report rebalance-recommendation-lifecycle title: Rebalance Recommendation lifecycle entity: RebalanceRecommendation chart: bar x: state y: records help: A proposed correction to portfolio allocation drift. Where rebalance recommendations sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'detected' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'analysed', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'proposed', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'executing', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'completed', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'failed', 6) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rebalance_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report rebalance-recommendation-top-reason title: Rebalance Recommendations: the most common reason entity: RebalanceRecommendation chart: bar x: reason y: records help: A proposed correction to portfolio allocation drift. The ten most frequent values of reason among rebalance recommendations; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(reason, '(blank)') AS reason, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rebalance_recommendation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report performance-snapshot-market-value-per-month title: Average market value per month (Performance Snapshot) entity: PerformanceSnapshot chart: line x: month y: average_market_value help: A dated set of portfolio valuation and return measures. The average market value of performance snapshots created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(market_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_market_value FROM bus_performance_snapshot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report performance-snapshot-absolute-return-per-month title: Average absolute return per month entity: PerformanceSnapshot chart: line x: month y: average_absolute_return help: A dated set of portfolio valuation and return measures. The average absolute return of performance snapshots created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(absolute_return)::numeric, 2) AS average_absolute_return FROM bus_performance_snapshot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report performance-snapshot-xirr-per-month title: Average xirr per month entity: PerformanceSnapshot chart: line x: month y: average_xirr help: A dated set of portfolio valuation and return measures. The average xirr of performance snapshots created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(xirr)::numeric, 2) AS average_xirr FROM bus_performance_snapshot WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report client-review-by-status title: Client Reviews by status entity: ClientReview chart: pie x: status y: records help: A dated adviser review of a client's portfolio, goals and risk context. How client reviews divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_review WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report client-review-by-goal-status title: Client Reviews by goal status entity: ClientReview chart: pie x: goal_status y: records help: A dated adviser review of a client's portfolio, goals and risk context. How client reviews divide across goal status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(goal_status::text, '(unset)') AS goal_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_review WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report client-review-lifecycle title: Client Review lifecycle entity: ClientReview chart: bar x: state y: records help: A dated adviser review of a client's portfolio, goals and risk context. Where client reviews sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'due' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'scheduled', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'conducted', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'follow_up', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 4) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_client_review WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report fee-schedule-by-status title: Fee Schedules by status entity: FeeSchedule chart: pie x: status y: records help: A named basis for charging a fee, including its type, rate and recurrence. How fee schedules divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_fee_schedule WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report fee-schedule-rate-by-status title: Total rate by status entity: FeeSchedule chart: bar x: status y: total_rate help: A named basis for charging a fee, including its type, rate and recurrence. Fee Schedules added up on rate, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(rate)::numeric, 2) AS total_rate FROM bus_fee_schedule WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report fee-schedule-top-fee-type title: Fee Schedules: the most common fee type entity: FeeSchedule chart: bar x: fee_type y: records help: A named basis for charging a fee, including its type, rate and recurrence. The ten most frequent values of fee type among fee schedules; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(fee_type, '(blank)') AS fee_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_fee_schedule WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report commission-by-status title: Commissions by status entity: Commission chart: pie x: status y: records help: Revenue earned in relation to a client and investment product. How commissions divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commission WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report commission-amount-by-status title: Total amount by status (Commission) entity: Commission chart: bar x: status y: total_amount help: Revenue earned in relation to a client and investment product. Commissions added up on amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_commission WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report commission-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month (Commission) entity: Commission chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: Revenue earned in relation to a client and investment product. The average amount of commissions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_commission WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report commission-reconciliation-by-status title: Commission Reconciliations by status entity: CommissionReconciliation chart: pie x: status y: records help: A comparison of expected commission with the amount received. How commission reconciliations divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commission_reconciliation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report commission-reconciliation-expected-amount-by-status title: Total expected amount by status entity: CommissionReconciliation chart: bar x: status y: total_expected_amount help: A comparison of expected commission with the amount received. Commission Reconciliations added up on expected amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(expected_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_expected_amount FROM bus_commission_reconciliation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report commission-reconciliation-expected-amount-per-month title: Average expected amount per month entity: CommissionReconciliation chart: line x: month y: average_expected_amount help: A comparison of expected commission with the amount received. The average expected amount of commission reconciliations created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(expected_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_expected_amount FROM bus_commission_reconciliation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
